# catingiran (`cti`) Configuration & User Guide

**catingiran** (`cti`) is a fast terminal IDE and code editor written in pure C featuring Vim-style modal editing and command line, top bufferline tabs, syntax highlighting (**C/C++**, **Python**, **Java**, JS/TS, Shell/Conf), a VS Code-style file explorer sidebar, a built-in **plugin manager**, split panes, code runner, project grep, fuzzy file finder, and Git integration.

---

## 1. Build, Install & Uninstall

```sh
git clone https://github.com/netanyahy/catingiran.git
cd catingiran
make
sudo make install
```

After installation:
* Both `cti` and `catingiran` commands are available in `/usr/local/bin`.
* Your editable preset config is created at `~/.config/catingiran/catingiran.conf`.
* Plugins live in `~/.config/catingiran/plugins/`.

To uninstall:
```sh
sudo make uninstall
```

---

## 2. Configuration (`catingiran.conf`)

Open your config right inside the editor with **`:conf`**:
```text
~/.config/catingiran/catingiran.conf
```
Reload config & plugins live at any time with **`:reload`**.

### `catingiran.conf` Options

| Option | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `theme` | `charcoal` | Theme: `charcoal`, `obsidian`, `catppuccin`, `tokyonight`, `nord`, `light` |
| `tab_size` | `4` | Tab width (`1`–`16`) |
| `expand_tab` | `true` | Insert spaces instead of `\t` |
| `line_numbers` | `true` | Show line numbers |
| `cursorline` | `true` | Highlight current line |
| `auto_indent` | `true` | Auto-indent new lines |
| `auto_pairs` | `true` | Auto-close `()`, `[]`, `{}`, `""`, `''` |
| `show_tabs` | `true` | Show top bufferline tabs |
| `mouse` | `true` | Enable mouse clicks & wheel scrolling |
| `sidebar_open` | `true` | Open file explorer sidebar on startup |
| `sidebar_width` | `28` | Sidebar width (`16`–`60`) |
| `show_hidden` | `true` | Show dotfiles in sidebar |
| `nerd_icons` | `true` | Nerd Font file/folder icons (`false` for ASCII/Unicode) |
| `output_height` | `8` | Bottom output drawer height in lines (`4`–`30`) |
| `git_branch` | `true` | Show Git branch in statusline |
| `russian_keymap` | `true` | Cyrillic support in Normal/Command mode (`ж` -> `:`, `р/о/л/д` -> `h/j/k/l`) |
| `plugin` | — | Add plugin: `plugin = user/repo` |

---

## 3. Built-in Plugin Manager (`catingiran Plug`)

Add plugins to `~/.config/catingiran/catingiran.conf`:
```ini
plugin = user/repo
```
Or install directly inside `cti` via `:PlugAdd user/repo`.

Plugin commands:
* `:PlugStatus` — view configured & installed plugins and registered commands.
* `:PlugInstall` — clone configured plugins into `~/.config/catingiran/plugins/`.
* `:PlugUpdate` — update installed plugins via `git pull`.
* `:PlugClean` — remove plugins no longer listed in `catingiran.conf`.
* `:PlugAdd user/repo` — append plugin to `catingiran.conf` and install it immediately.

---

## 4. Command Line (`:`) & Shortcuts (`<Space>` = Leader)

* `:conf` / `:reload` — open `catingiran.conf` / reload config & plugins.
* `:run` / `F5` / `Space + r` — compile & run current C/C++/Python/Java/Shell/Makefile file.
* `:out` / `:ho` / `Ctrl + J` — show / hide / toggle bottom output drawer.
* `:term` / `Space + t` — open interactive `$SHELL` and return back into `cti` on exit.
* `:find` / `Ctrl + P` / `Space + ff` — fuzzy file finder across project.
* `:grep <text>` / `Space + fg` — project-wide search (`Enter` or `gf` jumps to match).
* `:git` / `:diff` / `Space + g` — Git status/log or unstaged diff.
* `:stats` — project code statistics (files by language, lines, size, TODO/FIXME).
* `:vsplit` / `:split` / `:only` / `Ctrl + W` — split panes & switch active pane.
* `gcc` / `gc` (Visual) — toggle line comments (`//` or `#`).
* `J` / `K` (Visual) — move selected lines down / up.
* `m` / `M` — toggle bookmark (`★`) / jump to next bookmark.
* `:ot` / `:ht` / `:tree` / `Ctrl + B` / `F2` — open / hide / toggle file explorer.
* `:t1..:t9` / `Tab` / `Shift + Tab` — switch tabs.
* `:theme <name>` / `:themes` — switch theme live.
